<title>CHINA: Shanghai Friendship 96 net up 73.49 pct.</title>
<headline>Shanghai Friendship 96 net up 73.49 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(millions of yuan unless stated, against 1995 figures)</p>
<p> Turnover		581.774	vs	538.979</p>
<p> Net profit	    49.120	 vs	 28.314</p>
<p> Net asset per share  3.04 yuan   vs	  3.5 yuan</p>
<p> Earnings per share   0.44 yuan   vs	 0.28 yuan</p>
<p>Company name: Shanghai Friendship &amp; Overseas Chinese Co Ltd</p>
<p>Note: the results were announced in a company statement. All figures are based on domestic accounting standards.</p>
<p>Figures based on international accounting standards were not available.</p>
<p>The company's board of directors proposed a cash dividend of 0.15 yuan per share and a three-for-10 bonus issue, pending approval at a shareholders' meeting, the statement said.</p>
</text>
